            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Heavy 1, Blast (3&quot;), Concussive, Haywire, Graviton Pulse</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Extra Info" typeId="a165-1a07-fe23-3796"/>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Graviton Pulse" id="1c2d-e98d-7cfb-3284" hidden="false" page="251" publicationId="578f-d512-pubN123092">
          <description>Instead of rolling To Wound normally with this weapon, any model caught under the Blast template must instead roll equal to or under their Strength score on a D6 or suffer a wound (a roll of 6 always counts as a failure). After the Graviton pulse weapon has been fired, leave the Blast marker in place. This area now counts as both difficult terrain and dangerous terrain for the next player turn, thanks to the graviton flux.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
